<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tian Shi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> Shi was a member of the royal Tian family of Qi who became king of Qi during the rising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>. In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> moved him to the minor kingdom of Jiaodong on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> peninsula. His uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-rong">Tian Rong</a> refused the settlement, and when Tian Shi went to Jiaodong, Tian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong</a> pursued and killed him.</p></div>
